	CLEARDEVICE Command Switches
	
	The section "Universal CLI Switches," earlier in this chapter, describes
	switches /1, /2, /L, /L=pathname, and /Q, which you can use with all
	commands.  This section also explains the CLI32 switch /STR=.

     |  /RCNTL   Initiates Dump/Reboot of controller associated with the device.
     |               (AOS/VS II only)
     |
     |  /RENG    Initiates Dump/Reboot of engine associated with the device.
     |               (AOS/VS II only)
     |
	/RXON    Simulates a CTRL-Q (X-ON) character from the device (printer).

	/SBREAK  Sends a break signal to an IAC device.


	CLEARDEVICE Example

	You type the following command.

	) QPRINT/QUEUE=LQP/COPIES=10  MYFILE
	
	The letter-quality printer begins to print.  Then it exhausts its paper
	supply and goes off line.

	The system operator replenishes the paper, puts the printer back on
	line; and then goes to system console and uses the CONTROL command to
	discover the printer devicename.  The operator then uses the
	CLEARDEVICE command to clear the device and allow the printer to resume
	printing.  Dialog at the system console follows.

	) CONTROL @EXEC SPOOLSTATUS LQP
	LQP being porocessed by @CON3
	From EXEC ...
	
	) CLEARDEVICE/RXON  @CON3

