	Loading Microcode

     |  If you omit the /EXISTING and /MCODEFILE switches, the system will first
     |  determine whether the processor supports the loading of microcode after
     |  power-up.  If so, AOS/VS loads a default microcode file based on the
     |  CPUID of the job processor.  Otherwise, AOS/VS uses the microcode that
     |  was loaded on the job processor during power-up of the system.
     |
     |  The following systems load microcode at power-up time only, and do not
     |  allow loading of microcode with the JPINIT command:
     |  MV/25000, MV/30000, MV/35000, MV/40000, and MV/60000.
     |
     |  The /EXISTING switch may be used to specify use of the microcode that
     |  is already loaded into the job processor.  This switch is not necessary
     |  for those systems which only load microcode at power-up time.
     |
     |  The /MCODEFILE=pathname switch may be used to specify loading a specific
     |  microcode file (other than the default).  The value of this switch
     |  is the pathname of the microcode file you want to load.

